 <operand_table><table unique="1261429">
   <col width="62.892pt"/>
   <col width="215.78544pt"/>
   <col width="231.53616pt"/>
   <thead><tr>
     <th valign="middle"><para unique="1261431">Op/En</para>
      </th>
     <th valign="middle"><para unique="1261433">Operand 1</para>
      </th>
     <th valign="middle"><para unique="1261435">Operand 2</para>
      </th>
     </tr>
    </thead><tbody>
    <tr>
     <td valign="middle"><para unique="1261437">RM</para>
      </td>
     <td valign="middle"><para unique="1261439">ModRM:reg (w)</para>
      </td>
     <td valign="middle"><para unique="1261441">ModRM:r/m (r)</para>
      </td>
     </tr>
    <tr>
     <td valign="middle"><para unique="1261443">MR</para>
      </td>
     <td valign="middle"><para unique="1261445">ModRM:r/m (w, ModRM:[7:6] must not be 11b)</para>
      </td>
     <td valign="middle"><para unique="1261447">ModRM:reg (r)</para>
      </td>
     </tr>
    <tr>
     <td valign="middle"><para unique="1261449">RR</para>
      </td>
     <td valign="middle"><para unique="1261451">ModRM:reg (w)</para>
      </td>
     <td valign="middle"><para unique="1261453">ModRM:r/m (r, ModRM:[7:6] must be 11b) </para>
      </td>
     </tr>
    </tbody>
   <caption unique="1261454">Instruction Operand Encoding</caption>
   </table>
  </operand_table>
 <longdesc><para unique="1261456">Copies values from the source operand (second operand) to the destination operand (first operand). The source and destination operands can be mask registers, memory location or general purpose. The instruction cannot be used to transfer data between general purpose registers and or memory locations.</para>
  <para unique="1261457">When moving to a mask register, the result is zero extended to MAX_KL size (i.e., 64 bits currently). When moving to a general-purpose register (GPR), the result is zero-extended to the size of the destination. In 32-bit mode, the default GPR destination&#8217;s size is 32 bits. In 64-bit mode, the default GPR destination&#8217;s size is 64 bits. Note that VEX.W can only be used to modify the size of the GPR operand in 64b mode.</para>
  </longdesc>
 <operation>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1261459">KMOVW</title>
   <programlisting>IF *destination is a memory location*
	DEST[15:0] := SRC[15:0]
IF *destination is a mask register or a GPR *
	DEST := ZeroExtension(SRC[15:0])</programlisting>
   </section>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1261465">KMOVB</title>
   <programlisting>IF *destination is a memory location*
	DEST[7:0] := SRC[7:0]
IF *destination is a mask register or a GPR *
	DEST := ZeroExtension(SRC[7:0])</programlisting>
   </section>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1261471">KMOVQ</title>
   <programlisting>IF *destination is a memory location or a GPR*
	DEST[63:0] := SRC[63:0]
IF *destination is a mask register*
	DEST := ZeroExtension(SRC[63:0])</programlisting>
   </section>
  <section level="7">
   <title unique="1261477">KMOVD</title>
   <programlisting>IF *destination is a memory location*
	DEST[31:0] := SRC[31:0]
IF *destination is a mask register or a GPR *
	DEST := ZeroExtension(SRC[31:0])</programlisting>
   </section>
  </operation>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <programlisting>KMOVW __mmask16 _mm512_kmov(__mmask16 a);</programlisting>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Flags Affected">
  <para unique="1261485">None.</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="SIMD Floating-Point Exceptions">
  <para unique="1261487">None.</para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Other Exceptions">
  <para unique="1261491" format="xIndent1">Instructions with RR operand encoding, see <link unique="1261490" linkend="&lt;c&gt;__sdm_vol2A_ch02.fm#42536: 06_Table: Table 2-63. TYPE K20 Exception Definition (VEX-Encoded OpMask" xrefstyle="Table All - no page-period">Table&#160;2&#8209;65, &#8220;TYPE K20 Exception Definition (VEX-Encoded OpMask Instructions w/o Memory Arg).&#8221;</link></para>
  <para unique="1261495" format="xIndent1">Instructions with RM or MR operand encoding, see <link unique="1261494" linkend="&lt;c&gt;__sdm_vol2A_ch02.fm#68406: 06_Table: Table 2-22. Exception Definition (VEX-Encoded GPR Instructions)" xrefstyle="Table All - no page-period">Table&#160;2&#8209;66, &#8220;TYPE K21 Exception Definition (VEX-Encoded OpMask Instructions Addressing Memory).&#8221;</link></para>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
